    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI changed the `customerCode` format to `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` and everything derived from it now rebuilds on the new value.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** (the sole generator):\n- `nextCustomerCode` now takes both `city` and `lastName`. It builds `CITY3` (upper-cased first 3 letters of city), `LAST3` (upper-cased first 3 of last name), and `NNNN` as a **per-city** 4-digit sequence \u2014 one more than the owners already in that city (counting existing owners whose city matches case-insensitively, consistent with the existing `normalizeName` convention). Extracted a small `prefix3` helper since the 3-letter logic is now used twice.\n- The call site in `addOwner` passes `owner.getCity()` alongside the last name.\n- `membershipNumber` needed no change \u2014 it embeds `owner.getCustomerCode()` verbatim, so it automatically produces the new form (e.g. `SYD-SMI-0007-M26`).\n\n**`openapi.yml`**: updated the `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` descriptions and examples to match the new format.\n\n**Tests**: `AcceptanceTest.coreCustomerCodeHasCityPrefix` (asserting the `[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}` shape) now passes, and `./mvnw test` reports `BUILD SUCCESS` \u2014 `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` (the only concrete test class in the suite; `AcceptanceBase` is abstract and `AuditLogCapture` is a helper).",
